Root cause:
The bug was caused by the logic in the FreqProxTermsWriter class where a terms enumeration (termsEnum) could incorrectly be set to a non-null value even when the field for which the term was being deleted did not exist, leading to incorrect deletion of documents. Specifically, if a term was associated with one field (e.g., "b") and a delete operation was attempted on a different field (e.g., "a"), the code erroneously allowed the matching term to interfere with unrelated fields. The patch adds a check to ensure that if a terms object for the specific field is not found, the termsEnum is set to null, preventing this incorrect behavior.
